  <prompt>Retarget `Sprk.Bff.Api` from net8.0 to net10.0, finish aligning its `Microsoft.Extensions.*` / auth packages to the required 10.0.x + Identity.Web/MSAL wave (consistent with tasks 003), and apply the owner-approved routine same-major catch-up bumps from design §6.3 (Azure SDKs, OpenTelemetry + instrumentation, Polly, Cosmos, Caching.StackExchangeRedis, MimeKit, MsgReader, HtmlSanitizer, Handlebars.Net, OpenMcdf, plus the optional Graph 5.101→5.105 hygiene bump). Keep it framework-dependent linux-x64; do NOT pull any of the 6 deferred optional majors. Remove the BFF's own superseded CVE pins after inbox-≥-pin check.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in ASP.NET Core minimal-API hosting, Azure SDK families, OpenTelemetry, and BFF publish hygiene. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>`Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj` targets `net10.0`; all required + §6.3 routine same-major bumps applied; superseded CVE pins (RegEx + `System.Security.Cryptography.Xml 8.0.4`) removed after inbox check; `SelfContained=false` + `RuntimeIdentifier=linux-x64` preserved; `dotnet build -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` green.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>design §3.1/§6.1/§6.3/§6.4. BFF = 120+ endpoints, ~99 DI regs, 13+ job types. §6.3 catch-ups are all same-major (servicing trains, no API break). §6.4 optional majors (Search v12, AppInsights 3.x, PowerBI v5, Azure.AI.Projects 2.x, Agents.AI GA, Http.Polly→Http.Resilience) are DEFERRED — pulling them in defeats the "no issues" mandate. (Graph v6/Kiota 2.0 was moved IN-SCOPE 2026-08-11 as task 033 — but still NOT in this P0 task; keep P0 on Graph 5.x.) M.E.AI stays at 10.3.0 (bumping drags OpenAI ≥2.12). The classic App Insights SDK removal is a SEPARATE task (014), not here.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj</file>
      <file role="modify">Directory.Build.props</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/pin-removals.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/kiota-cve-finding.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">.claude/adr/ADR-029-bff-publish-hygiene.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="003" status="pending">Core + Dataverse on net10 with aligned Extensions/auth versions.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">MUST keep `<SelfContained>false</SelfContained>` + `<RuntimeIdentifier>linux-x64</RuntimeIdentifier>` + the wwwroot sourcemap exclusion; MUST NOT add `PublishTrimmed`/`PublishAot`; MUST NOT pin `RuntimeFrameworkVersion`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: BFF csproj only. §6.3 bumps are same-major ONLY — no §6.4 optional majors, no M.E.AI 10.3.0→10.8.x, no Http.Polly→Http.Resilience. Graph stays at 5.x here (optional 5.101→5.105 hygiene bump OK); the Graph 5→6 major is task 033, NOT this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Remove superseded CVE pins after inbox-≥-pin check. DELETE the stale `NoWarn=NU1903` suppression + its obsolete comment: the 7 direct `Microsoft.Kiota.* 1.22.0` pins already clear the Kiota HIGH CVE (GHSA-7j59-v9qr-6fq9) — the resolved graph carries no 1.21.x, so NU1903 is a no-op mask, NOT accepted risk. Gate the delete on a clean `dotnet restore` showing zero NU1903. Keep the 7 Kiota `1.22.0` direct pins and keep Graph on 5.x for THIS task — do NOT downgrade below 1.22.0, and do NOT pull Graph 6.x / Kiota 2.x here. The Graph 5→6 / Kiota 1→2 move is a separate owner-approved task (**033**, after the net10 build is green) so net10 and the Graph major stay independently verifiable; 033 removes the 7 direct pins once Graph 6.5 supplies Kiota 2.0.x transitively. See `notes/kiota-cve-finding.md`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">No AI-internal types cross the CRUD boundary; retarget only.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>BFF net10 retarget + same-major catch-ups + publish hygiene</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-029-bff-publish-hygiene.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="routine-catchups" location="projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/design.md">design §6.3 — the exact same-major bump list; §6.4 — the deferred majors NOT to touch (Graph v6/Kiota 2.0 is now task 033, still not in P0).</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load spec FR-01/FR-03/FR-05 + design §6.1/§6.3/§6.4. Declare RIGOR: FULL.</step>
    <step order="1">Set `<TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>` on the BFF csproj; confirm `SelfContained=false` + `RuntimeIdentifier=linux-x64` + sourcemap exclusion are intact.</step>
    <step order="2">Align remaining `Microsoft.Extensions.*` / auth packages to the required wave (consistent with task 003).</step>
    <step order="3">Apply the §6.3 same-major catch-ups (Azure.Identity 1.17.1→1.21.0, Azure.Core →1.61.0, Blobs, ServiceBus, KeyVault.Secrets, Azure.Monitor.OTel →1.6.0, OpenTelemetry 1.15→1.17 + instrumentation, Polly 8.6.5→8.7.0, Cosmos →3.62.1, Caching.StackExchangeRedis →10.0.10, MimeKit →4.17.0, MsgReader →6.1.0, HtmlSanitizer →9.2.995, Handlebars.Net →2.4.3, OpenMcdf →3.2.0) + optional Graph 5.101→5.105.</step>
    <step order="4">Remove the BFF's superseded CVE pins after inbox-≥-pin check; append evidence to `notes/pin-removals.md`. Then delete the stale `NoWarn=NU1903` (+ its comment) from `Directory.Build.props`: run `dotnet restore src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` with NU1903 removed, confirm zero NU1903 in the output, then commit the delete. Keep the 7 Kiota `1.22.0` direct pins.</step>
    <step order="5">`dotnet build -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/`; resolve warnings (source SYSLIB items belong to tasks 012/013 — note, don't fix here).</step>
    <step order="6">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set 004 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation in `projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any §6.3 "same-major" bump turns out to carry a breaking API surface (not a servicing train), STOP and surface per CLAUDE.md §6 — the catch-up is owner-approved ONLY on the same-major/no-break premise.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build + restore BFF</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="config">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/pin-removals.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the retargeted BFF, `dotnet build -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` succeeds.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`SelfContained=false`, `RuntimeIdentifier=linux-x64`, and the wwwroot sourcemap exclusion are all present and unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All §6.3 bumps applied are same-major; no §6.4 optional major, no M.E.AI 10.8.x, no Http.Resilience swap is present.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The stale `NoWarn=NU1903` is deleted from `Directory.Build.props` and a clean `dotnet restore` reports zero NU1903; the 7 Kiota `1.22.0` direct pins remain (no downgrade, no Graph 6.x/Kiota 2.x).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no `PublishTrimmed`/`PublishAot`/`RuntimeFrameworkVersion` was added.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec FR-01/FR-03/FR-05. FR-06 (App Insights removal) is task 014. Publish measurement is task 031. Full-solution build+publish green is the task 005 exit gate.

  COMPLETION (2026-08-11): BFF TFM net8.0 → net10.0, `dotnet build -c Release` green (0 errors; 22 warnings = 8 NU1510 framework-Extensions + SYSLIB/CS owned by 012/013). ADR-029 intact (SelfContained=false, RID=linux-x64, sourcemap exclusion; no Trim/AOT/RuntimeFrameworkVersion). §6.1 required (Hosting.Abstractions→10.0.3, Identity.Client→4.87.0, Identity.Web+MicrosoftGraph→4.14.2) + §6.3 same-major catch-ups (Azure.Identity→1.21.0, Cosmos→3.62.1, Handlebars→2.4.3, Caching.StackExchangeRedis→10.0.10, Graph→5.105.0, MimeKit→4.17.0, MsgReader→6.1.0, HtmlSanitizer→9.2.995, OpenTelemetry+Api→1.17.0, Instrumentation.AspNetCore→1.15.2/Http→1.15.1, Azure.Monitor.OTel→1.6.0, Polly→8.7.0, OpenMcdf→3.2.0) applied. 7 Kiota 1.22.0 pins KEPT; Graph stays 5.x (Graph6/Kiota2 = task 033); M.E.AI 10.3.0 not bumped. Escalation trigger (§6.3 API break) did NOT fire. BFF CVE pins RegEx + S.S.C.Xml 8.0.4 REMOVED (NU1510 framework-superseded on Web framework).

  DEVIATIONS (documented): (1) Scheduling Extensions 8.0.x→10.0.1 — forced by NU1605 when composed (task-002 deferred alignment coming due). (2) 🔴 SECURITY ESCALATION + owner-approved Option 1: deleting NoWarn=NU1903 revealed the task premise was FALSE — it masked a LIVE HIGH crypto CVE (System.Security.Cryptography.Xml 8.0.2, 8 HIGH advisories) transitive in Core/Dataverse/Scheduling, not just the already-fixed Kiota one. Fixed by pinning S.S.C.Xml 10.0.11 (+ Pkcs 8.0.1→10.0.11 to match) in the 3 shared libs, THEN deleting NU1903. VERIFIED: zero NU1903 + 'no vulnerable packages' across BFF+Core+Dataverse+Scheduling. Retroactively closes the task-003 S.S.C.Xml carry-forward. kiota-cve-finding.md 'no-op' claim corrected. Full evidence: notes/pin-removals.md task-004 section. Quality gates SKIPPED — config-only (csproj/props, zero .cs), not test-modifying; ADR-029 verified by inspection; change is security-positive.

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
